# 1-based lines to bookmark, one per line.
#
# The sample uses the BRACED package form. `package app.billing` on its own line
# parses as a `package_clause` that encloses nothing, so it could never appear
# in a breadcrumb; the braced form does enclose, which makes `package_clause` an
# observed container and puts a package level on every trail below.
#
# Match arms and if-branches are given different shapes on purpose: identical
# sibling statements make the generated structural query ambiguous and codemark
# refuses the bookmark. A sample-authoring constraint, not a profile defect.

# Inside a concrete method on a trait — proves `trait_definition` contains a
# definition and not only an abstract signature.
41

# Inside a guarded match arm inside the for comprehension in compute(). The
# deepest chain here: package > class > def > for > match > arm.
59

# Inside the local `def rounded` declared in compute()'s body — a definition
# nested in a method, which a parser corpus has no reason to produce.
66

# Inside render() in the nested `class Summary` — proves type-in-type
# containment: package > class > class > def.
91

# Inside the companion `object Invoice`.
105

# Inside `def money` on `object Formatting`.
121

# Inside `object Debug` nested in `object Formatting` — object-in-object.
127

# NOT bookmarkable, recorded rather than silently omitted:
#
#   57    case LineItem(_, amount, true) => amount * TaxRate
#   78    true
#
# A match arm's own line has no landmark between it and the enclosing def, so
# the query cannot anchor inside the arm and collides with its siblings. The
# targets above sit on a uniquely shaped statement *within* an arm instead.
# Same class of limitation as codemark#239.
